WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.520
States are going to be making decisions very
soon about whether we are continuing the lockdown,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.759
shut downs.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:07.759
Stay at home.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:11.550
Social distancing guidelines or whether things
are going to start being loosened.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.419
Now, some states never really shut down.

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:17.550
Cities within those states may have taken
measures, but there are states that never

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.550
did anything.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.710
So I'm not really talking about them.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:25.000
But as an example, here in Massachusetts,
officially, we are closed until May 4th, which

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.000
is next Monday.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.140
Charlie Baker, the Republican governor who's
been doing a pretty OK job handling things,

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.860
said that sometime this week he will have
guidance about what is coming next.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.050
And there's speculation in a lot of states
about are we going until May 15th?

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.210
Some states already have.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.270
Are we going until May 30?

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.960
First, a couple of states already have at
least some degree.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.130
What is the next step?

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:50.000
And I think that as we think about this next
phase, we need to be very real about one element

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.990
of this, which I think informs what needs
to be done.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:01:00.210
And it's recognizing that there are many Americans
that are not going to tolerate much more of

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:06.830
what I would call a full shutdown with as
many business closures as we have, as much

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.890
social distancing as we have.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.430
And to the degree that we've had it in some
states really for a month and a half or closing

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.330
in on two months at this point in time.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.320
But I want to be really clear as I talk about
this, I'm not saying open it up and let it

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.400
rip the way protesters want.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.620
I'm not saying any of that.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.040
And I'm not saying that we shouldn't be doing
what we are doing.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.040
What

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:34.810
I'm saying is I think that it would be useful
to find small ways of at least making it feel

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:41.810
like we're taking steps in order to ensure
more people actually adhere to the most important

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.970
elements of these guidelines.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:48.810
So the point of the segment is I want to be
truthful, which is tens of millions of Americans

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:54.690
are more or less at their limit or close to
it, either psychologically or economically.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:02:01.590
And I believe that we are getting closer to
the end of governors being able to say everything

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:06.479
stays closed before people start ignoring
more and more of these guidelines.

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.310
So the basis of this commentary is essentially
harm reduction.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.240
Some states are extended through May 15.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:21.530
There are other states that are formally shut
down until the end of this month and then

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.709
may or may not open.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:23.739
And I think there's kind of an

00:02:23.739 --> 00:02:30.090
invisible wall, an imaginary wall sometime
between May 15 and June 1, specially with

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.980
the weather getting nicer in many parts of
the country, where if a governor comes out

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:39.480
and says we're shut down until June 15, we're
shut down under July 1.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.129
I think it may backfire and that there will
be people who start to completely ignore it.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:47.940
So here's my idea, my recommendation.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.420
Governors could consider instead of saying
we're just going to extend the full, full

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:57.360
shutdown until June 1 or we're going to extend
a full shutdown until June 15 or even July

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.360
1, which will cause a lot of frustration for
many people.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.500
I would had advised governors to instead say,
I hear the frustration.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.720
People are psychologically and economically
exhausted from this.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.099
So let me help you.

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:15.050
And the point here is we want to prevent reactions
of another month.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.050
Screw it.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:21.610
I'll do whatever I want and instead create
a reaction of, hey, here's another month during

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:26.459
which here are three new things that are being
extended or opened up to me.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:27.459
I can do it.

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:28.459
I can keep wearing the mask.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:30.090
I can get, you know, all that stuff.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:35.720
So the idea is let's go really hard until
call it May 15th as an example, if you help

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:36.740
me.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.840
Governors could say and stay inside as much
as possible.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.400
Use masks when you're out.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.390
Always stay six feet apart from people at
grocery stores if you do all that stuff on

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.970
May 15th.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.170
Here are the three things I think we will
be able to do.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:56.239
The three things don't have to be huge, but
they should be something because the problem

00:03:56.239 --> 00:04:02.620
of doing March 15th to 30 first and then being
told now it's all of April and then

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.680
being told it's now all of May is it doesn't
feel like anything is happening.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.920
And people are growing increasingly frustrated.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.349
Even people who understand that we have to
be doing this and there are reasons for why

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:14.769
we are doing it.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:17.969
So I don't have the exact answers.

00:04:17.969 --> 00:04:19.729
I don't think Jim's should be open.

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:21.939
Trump included Jim's on phase one of his reopening
plan.

00:04:21.939 --> 00:04:23.259
I don't think that makes any sense.

00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:25.349
I think that's a bad idea.

00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:31.800
Could you say with the weather getting nicer
places that have outdoor seating, you can

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.330
essentially let people have their take out
at the outdoor seating?

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.830
No waiter service.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.599
You've got to reduce the density of the seating.

00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:42.520
So, you know, maybe tables are 10 feet apart.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.869
Would that be something with that?

00:04:43.869 --> 00:04:49.400
That would be thousands, maybe tens of thousands
of restaurants where people who have been

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.400
just getting takeout

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.259
and taking it can bring the takeout to an
outdoor table, sit there and have it.

00:04:55.259 --> 00:04:57.120
No waiter or waitress service.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.900
Would that psychologically help?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.680
Maybe provide a little bit of a boost to restaurants.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.169
Maybe, I don't know.

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:08.419
Could you say movie theaters with masks mandatory?

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:12.569
Could open at 10 percent capacity, which means,
you know, there's plenty of room for people

00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:15.270
to be very far apart.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:18.729
Social distancing in line to buy tickets and
no concession stands.

00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:19.729
I don't know.

00:05:19.729 --> 00:05:20.729
Would people even go?

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:21.729
Would people want that?

00:05:21.729 --> 00:05:22.729
I'm not really sure.

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:28.469
I'm thinking out loud here for the social
distancing component between friends and family.

00:05:28.469 --> 00:05:35.360
Could they say outdoor gatherings in your
backyard or in the park or whatever with masks

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:41.199
among people not in high risk groups who have
had no symptoms and continue to have no symptoms

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:43.410
as long as you stay six feet apart?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.939
Would that feel like a win, given how things
have been for four, six, seven, close to eight

00:05:47.939 --> 00:05:48.939
weeks?

00:05:48.939 --> 00:05:49.939
At this point in time, I don't know.

00:05:49.939 --> 00:05:51.080
I'm thinking out loud here.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:57.099
But my point is, if is on April 30th, say
we're now extending till May thirty first.

00:05:57.099 --> 00:06:01.729
I believe the frustration will push a lot
of people to abandon all the guidelines and

00:06:01.729 --> 00:06:03.340
that would be really bad.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.669
Instead, if we can feel like there's progress.

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:09.819
Imagine the governor says we made it to April
30th.

00:06:09.819 --> 00:06:10.869
Thank you.

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:14.300
New cases are down, but they're still too
high to reopen.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:19.520
I have determined we are going not to phase
one, but to phase zero point one.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:25.339
And here are three things that I am saying
we can do carefully from May 1st to the 15th.

00:06:25.339 --> 00:06:28.770
I'll check back in with you in 15 days and
see if we can do anything else.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.619
The feeling that things are improving could
actually get people, people to more closely

00:06:33.619 --> 00:06:36.520
abide by masks, work from home.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:37.930
All that stuff.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:44.550
And then we we may be better off overall than
creating frustration and abandonment of the

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.720
guidelines.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.939
Thinking out loud.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:07:18.919
Let me know

00:07:18.919 --> 00:07:53.659
what

00:07:53.659 --> 00:08:08.430
you think.

